d}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272163 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a7a2955a-d0ed-5f0b-a82c-5ef03bbf9550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272163 #edb/ref 1074 "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6-5+4 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272165 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272165 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140853" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272165 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272165 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272165 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d1823b0b-dd9b-5b00-861c-14c6a4bab473" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272165 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =30+6-15+0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272166 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272166 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140861" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592